WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.898
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.670
JEFFREY PURITT:
Morning everybody.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.530
It's truly my pleasure to be
here today to briefly discuss

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.860
my favorite topic, my
TELUS International family,

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.680
as well as to share with you a
little bit about how Google has

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.760
helped to enable our success.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.560
By a show of hands,
how many of you

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.939
has ever solved a Rubik's cube?

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:35.230
I thought it would be everybody
in this room, actually.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.050
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.160
Maybe not Jim.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.310
Did you know that the world
record for the fastest Rubik's

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:45.510
cube solve is 4.904
seconds and that it's

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.800
held by a 14-year-old
boy from Kentucky?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.470
What I find most
fascinating about that,

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:54.560
no, not that he's from
Kentucky, but rather

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.270
the actual number
of permutations that

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:02.230
are possible-- 43 quintillion.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:06.630
That's a 43 followed
by 18 zeroes.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.100
And all based on
the decisions one

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.810
makes on how to twist and turn
the 54 elements of the cube.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:18.260
42 years after its invention,
I believe this fascinating cube

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.580
is a great analogy for the
growth and success of TELUS

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.180
International.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.010
As you just heard briefly in
[INAUDIBLE] kind introduction,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.160
our company has
grown exponentially.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.840
Since our inception in 2005,
starting with just 1500 team

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:38.520
members, one location in Manila
providing support in English

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.664
only, I'm proud to say
that 11 years later we have

00:01:42.664 --> 00:01:45.080
what I believe to be the best
team in the business process

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.100
outsourcing industry.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.150
Our 25,000 team members serve
some of the world's most

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:56.860
iconic brands across high tech,
retail, gaming, e-commerce,

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.330
health care, travel, finance,
and telecom from state

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.480
of the art facilities in North
America, Central America,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.720
Europe, and Asia.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.259
Our recent $1 billion
enterprise value

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:13.120
is predicated upon
our proven formula.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.860
We carefully select and invest
in companies whose values

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.560
are aligned with ours, who
have teams that welcome

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.440
and celebrate
diversity, in leadership

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.640
that leads by example, and
in people who respect others.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.150
While we've only made
three acquisitions, one

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.180
in each of Asia, Central
America, and Eastern Europe,

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.620
and each of those businesses had
fewer than 1,500 team members

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.830
at the time of our
original investment,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.070
our real challenge
was harmonizing

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:49.716
these similar, but distinct,
corporate cultures.

00:02:49.716 --> 00:02:51.590
Each of those teams took
a different approach

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.690
to recruitment and
on-boarding, to communication

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.180
and collaboration, to
performance management

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.270
and reporting.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.500
Utilizing diverse operating
models, tool, systems,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.390
and technologies to
ensure we realized

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.700
the requisite synergies from
acquiring and integrating

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.400
these disparate groups and to
support our aspirational growth

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.510
whilst consistently delivering
a best in class client and team

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.040
member experience, we needed
to think and act differently.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.870
After all, according to the
literature, 70% of acquisitions

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.470
actually destroy
shareholder value.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.590
So my story isn't about where
TELUS International is today,

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.690
it's about how we
arrived here, how

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.010
we overcame these challenges,
and most importantly,

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:39.800
how we plan to execute
upon our ambitious goal

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.410
to more than double the
size of our business

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.300
in the next five years or less.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.610
And this is where Google
and their incomparable suite

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.360
of business tools
come into play.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.400
So let's imagine that
each one of the nine

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.190
squares on each side
of the Rubik's cube

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:58.230
represent a different
business function

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.620
that the teams and operations
in each of our delivery centers

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.330
brought to the table.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.320
Functions like HR practices,
recruitment, training,

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:10.450
learning development, sales,
marketing, communications,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.120
payroll reporting which all
culminated enabling our team

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.760
to execute upon more
than 175 million customer

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.720
interactions we manage annually
via voice chat, e-mail,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.300
and social media.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.650
The thought of how many
different tools, platforms,

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:29.520
processes, and how disconnected
we might be as an organization

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.380
was overwhelming.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.460
Remember the 43
quintillion permutations

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.880
I mentioned earlier.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.620
So we had to quickly and
effectively align our teams

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:38.950
on a global scale.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:42.320
And we found the perfect partner
with which to do so in Google.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.990
Deploying Google
Cloud based technology

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.250
enabled us to standardize
how we did business

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.970
across our entire enterprise
and, in the process,

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.380
helped us to collaborate
and innovate,

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.060
promoted agile thinking
and actually increased

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.640
our team member engagement.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.110
So how, you may ask?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.980
Well, we know that
our team members

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.420
are our greatest
competitive advantage, which

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:06.250
is why we've cultivated a
unique caring culture that's

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:10.680
driving industry leading
engagement, attrition

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.790
rates, and scores
that are better

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.860
than the competition
which, in turn, led

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.550
to better performance and
increased top line client

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.080
growth.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.370
We call this the
Culture Value Chain.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.190
And as confirmed by
Frost and Sullivan,

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.360
we can now directly correlate
our unique corporate culture

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.920
with our industry
leading performance.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.850
So constant communication
and collaboration

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.810
amongst our team members
around the world is critical.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.810
Historically, teams
attempting to collaborate

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.860
across time zones
would inevitably

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.930
encounter issues with
timeliness and version control

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.000
of documents.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.840
Leveraging Google
Drive and Hangouts,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.050
our teams easily edit
documents, presentations

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.644
simultaneously and in real-time.

00:05:49.644 --> 00:05:51.310
They can quickly book
a video conference

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:54.290
from their desk inspiring
spirited teamwork

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.387
and continuous collaboration
and innovation.

00:05:57.387 --> 00:05:59.720
Additionally, our move to add
thousands of Google Chrome

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:03.430
boxes to our limited number
of Cisco TelePresence units

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.100
has made video conferencing
more readily available

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.940
and approachable, enabling
us to cost effectively

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.160
gather our team members for
training sessions, recognition

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.650
events, customer meetings,
business reviews, and even

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.976
board meetings.

00:06:15.976 --> 00:06:18.350
Also, by deploying Google
Chromebooks to our team leaders

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.300
on the floor in our
contact centers,

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.200
they now provide real time
feedback and on-the-spot

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.120
coaching to help their
team members grow

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.090
and succeed in their roles.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:30.300
The ROI has been impressive with
near instantaneous improvements

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.460
in our clients' key metrics
and happier, more engaged team

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:36.200
members who recognize
our investment

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.840
in their professional
development

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.470
and they stay with us longer
to grow their careers.

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:43.610
Finally, our pace of growth
makes business intelligence

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.630
even more critical to our
decision making process.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.680
Leveraging Google
Scripts and Sheets,

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.510
we developed and
deployed a unique cloud

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.820
based BI platform
which, in real time,

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.190
aggregates operational
data from multiple sources

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:59.610
like ACD, time reporting,
CRM, and quality applications.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.010
As a result, we now have
standardized operational

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:05.390
reporting across the globe that
provides deeper insights for us

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.070
and our clients.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.290
Even with our over 100
clients and terabytes of data,

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.410
our front-line team members can
instantly assess performance

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.160
and take corrective action to
help us proactively deliver

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.914
on our customers first promise.

00:07:18.914 --> 00:07:20.830
So as you can see, our
partnership with Google

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.710
has enabled us to
essentially speak

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.910
the same language in
so many different ways

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.480
which is, I think, all the more
a remarkable accomplishment

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:30.670
given that our agents
speak over 35 of them

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:33.202
on a daily basis
with our customers.

00:07:33.202 --> 00:07:34.660
And we're only just
getting started

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:38.190
as we've just got two new pilot
programs underway leveraging

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.560
the power of Google's
Machine Learning capabilities

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.450
to take a revolutionary
approach to real-time fraud

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:47.860
identification and PCI support
as well as contact reduction

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.470
and automation.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.790
When we're aligned as a
team and as an organization,

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:55.420
we have the white
space we need to be

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:58.890
agile and innovative to
focus on growing our business

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:03.200
and creating value for our
clients and importantly,

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:07.100
to do what is at the heart
of our caring culture,

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.950
to give back to the
citizens and communities

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:15.010
where our team members live,
work, and raise their families.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.750
Well, I'm so very, very proud
of what our team has already

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.190
accomplished in working
to make the world a better

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:24.090
place, having
contributed $336 million

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:27.380
to charitable and
not-for-profit organizations

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.110
and, more importantly,
provided almost seven

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.289
million hours of
volunteer service

00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:35.720
to local communities building
schools and homes, for example.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.710
There is still so much
more that needs to be done.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:41.980
I could not be more
excited by what's

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.770
ahead for TELUS
International and with Google

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.600
by our side as our trusted
technology partner,

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.592
I have no doubt we will achieve
our ambitious growth targets.

00:08:51.592 --> 00:08:53.650
It may, perhaps, take
just a little bit more

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.960
than the 4.9 seconds, however.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.960
Thank you all for your
time and attention today.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.060
I welcome the opportunity to
answer your questions, if any,

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:00.768
during the break.

00:09:00.768 --> 00:09:03.280
[APPLAUSE]

